23. The university-level abstraction
Let's formalize what we've learned.
A replicated database can be viewed as:
Logical state S
      |
      +----------------+
      |                |
      v                v
 Physical copy A    Physical copy B
The system must maintain some relationship:
A ≈ B
But what does ≈ mean?
Possibilities include:
Strong synchronization
A == B
before acknowledging a write.
Eventual synchronization
A ≠ B
temporarily, but:
eventually A == B
Quorum-based systems
Perhaps we require:
some subset of replicas
to agree before operations complete.
That one question—
"What relationship must exist between replicas?"
—is the gateway to the next lessons.
