   backup strategy          automation
   replica placement        recovery design
This is a very practical architecture framework.
________________________________________
57. Backup still matters after replication
Suppose:
Primary
  |
  +--> R1
  +--> R2
Someone accidentally executes:
DELETE FROM orders;
Replication copies the delete:
Primary: empty
R1: empty
R2: empty
Failover doesn't help.
You need:
backup / point-in-time recovery
So a robust system often has:
replicas → availability
backups  → historical recovery
