18. Cross-region async replication
Usually:
US Primary
     |
     | async
     +------> Europe
     |
     +------> India
Why async?
Because synchronous cross-region replication means:
India
  ↓
US
  ↓
India
and network latency becomes part of the write commit path.
If regions are geographically far apart, this can make write latency significantly higher.
Therefore many architectures choose:
local synchronous
+
cross-region asynchronous
This is a very common compromise.
________________________________________
19. The "local sync, global async" pattern
Imagine:
             Region A
          +-------------+
          | Primary     |
          |      |      |
          |      v      |
          |   Standby   |
          +-------------+
                 |
                 | async
                 v
             Region B
          +-------------+
          | Replica     |
          +-------------+
