54. Lesson 5 teaser: Split Brain
Imagine a 5-node cluster:
          A
       /  |  \
      B   C   D
           \
            E
Network partitions:
Partition 1: A B C
Partition 2: D E
A/B/C have:
3/5 → majority
D/E have:
2/5 → minority
So far, consensus handles this nicely.
But now imagine a badly designed system where D/E are also allowed to accept writes.
Then:
Partition 1:
Leader A
X = 100

Partition 2:
Leader D
X = 200
When the network heals:
A says X=100
D says X=200
Now:
Whose reality wins?
And it gets even nastier.
Imagine both sides believe they have leadership because of:
•	stale leader information 
•	bad failure detection 
•	incorrect quorum configuration 
•	network partition 
•	delayed messages 
•	incorrect fencing 
•	application-level routing caches 
That's split brain.
