You don't need formal distributed-systems mathematics yet, but remember this:
You cannot use a lease expiration mechanism to simultaneously guarantee indefinite client execution and automatic recovery from client failure.
If you want:
dead clients don't block forever
you need expiration.
If you have expiration:
live-but-paused clients may become stale
Therefore you need another mechanism if stale actions can cause damage.
That mechanism is fencing.
